# Rock Paper Scissors — web project conventions

## Stack

- Ship the game as **`index.html`**, **`style.css`**, and **`script.js`** at the project root unless the README explicitly adds a build step.
- Prefer standards-based APIs and minimal dependencies.

## Behavior (parity)

- Preserve the documented rules in `README.md`: random computer choice, tie +1 / win +2 / loss −1, play-again loop, final score on exit.
- Keep JavaScript easy to reason about: prefer named functions and clear separation of “pick outcome”, “update score”, and “UI refresh” concerns.

## UX and accessibility

- Support both pointer and keyboard use for choosing moves and confirming “play again” / quit.
- Expose round result, computer choice, and running score in the page—do not rely on the developer console for normal play.

## Scope

- Make small, purposeful changes; avoid refactoring unrelated repositories (including the sibling Java project) when working in this folder unless the user asks.
